    "narrative": "Our lineup for 2026-05-17 is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts our highest efficiency rating at 87.14. He holds a clear elite advantage against Lorenzen, compounded by a significant park factor and a favorable spot in the two-hole. **James Wood** (78.42) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) represent the next tier of high-floor production; **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned as a lead-off hitter facing a weak arm in Young, while **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a strong park factor and a clean middle-of-the-order opportunity against Houser. We are also capitalizing on the high-SB potential inherent in our roster, specifically leaning on **Brice Turang** and **Seiya Suzuki**; both face pitchers with slow deliveries, creating an opportunistic environment for our stolen base-focused strategy. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros**, whose 45.40 score hovered near the marginal threshold but ultimately could not displace the high-scoring floor of our starting infielders. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a park-adjusted bump against Soroka, his position at the bottom of the order and the lack of a platoon advantage relegated him to the pine. We are closely monitoring the matchup for **Cole Young** and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014at 50.19 and 50.07 respectively, they are the weakest links in our current set; should the game-day conditions shift or early-game momentum stall, they are the primary candidates for a mid-day pivot. Finally, we remain in a holding pattern regarding our injured core, with **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton** still occupying IL spots as we await medical clearance.",
